        {
            "behavior": "none",
            "id": "n620-2",
            "kind": "label",
            "label": "If you have vt print running on a remote terminal, you can print to that system by specifying that you wish to print to a socket and then specifying the host address and port.  For example, if the hostname is \"terminal1.mystore.lan\" and vt print is running on the default port, the Printer Address line would read \"socket:terminal1.mystore.lan,65530\".  Instead of specifying the port on the Printer Address line, you can also specify it via the Connection Interface button by selecting VT Daemon.",
            "legacy": {
                "kind": "ZONE_SIMPLE"
            },
