        {
            "behavior": "none",
            "id": "n620-1",
            "kind": "label",
            "label": "The old style of printing to parallel ports can still be used:  simply specify the portname, as \"lpt0\" for FreeBSD.  With the new method, you can specify the entire device file path, as \"parallel:/dev/lpt0\".  This may provide support for serial and USB printers as well, but we have not yet tested those.",
